Send the pod's image pull secrets to the plugin in the create request.

The kubelet reads the Secrets named in spec.imagePullSecrets and hands their
registry credentials to the image puller. The virtual kubelet put only the
Secrets that volumes mount into PodCreateRequests, so a plugin that pulls
images on remote capacity had no credentials unless it read Secrets from the
Kubernetes API itself, which needs its own RBAC and duplicates the virtual
kubelet's access. RemoteExecution now adds each referenced dockerconfigjson or
dockercfg Secret to PodCreateRequests.Secrets, once per name. Like the kubelet,
it logs a warning and continues when a pull secret is missing, unreadable, or
of another type.

Upstream status: not yet reported to interlink-hq/interLink.

